node_modules
dist
dist-ssr
*.local
# `.env` is NOT here on purpose. It is TRACKED, and it is meant to be: it carries this project's local
# default, VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8080, so a fresh clone runs against a local backend without
# anyone configuring anything. A rule here could not have changed that either -- git applies no ignore rule
# to a path it already tracks -- and the line that used to sit here read as protection while a live Google
# key sat in that same tracked file for months (register B2). Secrets and personal overrides go in
# `.env.local`, which `*.local` above covers and which is never committed.
.env.production
.env.development

